<Panels>
  <config><![CDATA[{
  "game_id": 73,
  "created_at": "2026-05-05T22:15:11.000Z",
  "level_num": "custom",
  "user_id": 1,
  "properties": {
    "panels": [
      {
        "key": "testlesson-coloring-with-potions-55895306-2df7-4265-ae41-0ae1efef7bc6",
        "text": "Harry, you've made a great start with your web page! But it looks a bit… plain, doesn't it?",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/a40037498f89156720e61a3bb88a9abf-testlesson-coloring-with-potions-panel-1-b75d48bf-5d02-4eda-ab44-916e55c80dfc.png",
        "layout": "text-top-left"
      },
      {
        "key": "testlesson-coloring-with-potions-32707eed-f488-47aa-9509-7273fd225ad3",
        "text": "Just like Snape's potions add special effects, we can use 'Potions' (called CSS) to add color and style to your page! It's like magic for your website!",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/e492be5f72f14eb965dd5d9fc714ba25-testlesson-coloring-with-potions-panel-2-737f7a1f-9f83-4060-8f30-9bf84c33698d.png",
        "layout": "text-top-center"
      },
      {
        "key": "testlesson-coloring-with-potions-49c6b2d5-4711-4d58-8e77-880560e061c3",
        "text": "First, we tell our 'potion' which part of the page to change. Do we want to color a word, a paragraph, or a whole section? This is called 'selecting' an element.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/533a5d3b645d7df741196f9a15f84312-testlesson-coloring-with-potions-panel-3-98d66d2f-9317-4efb-9844-a3dff04d744c.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-left"
      },
      {
        "key": "testlesson-coloring-with-potions-527b6b51-f66e-4a39-9081-1ccbc2fb9f84",
        "text": "To change the color of the *text* itself, we use the `color` potion! Let's make the word \"Welcome\" a bright Gryffindor red.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/14e9273d9cfe1df98cc323e51eda6490-testlesson-coloring-with-potions-panel-4-860826b3-5953-4a69-90e6-1c1adc9ae9c0.png",
        "layout": "text-top-right"
      },
      {
        "key": "testlesson-coloring-with-potions-4ae76d93-e2a2-40a5-8058-27dba199c0a9",
        "text": "And to change the *background* behind the text, we use the `background-color` potion! How about a shimmering house gold?",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/1fbaaf05e79230d96ca5b3edc4e7a10d-testlesson-coloring-with-potions-panel-5-2d1b2596-0034-48bd-8ba1-1f6a252e4f4b.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "key": "testlesson-coloring-with-potions-74816bed-c3f7-4cbc-b41e-c0bea24bbf90",
        "text": "With a few simple 'potions,' your webpage is starting to look truly magical! Keep experimenting with different colors and styles to make it uniquely yours!",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/742266e884ffec7ba98a3c2ab4da39d9-testlesson-coloring-with-potions-panel-6-a0fa5aaa-7429-4b4c-a4c8-4382b760c16a.png",
        "layout": "text-top-center"
      }
    ],
    "generate_prompt": "Explain how 'potions' (CSS) can be used to add color and style to a web page. Introduce the concept of selecting HTML elements and applying style properties like 'color' and 'background-color'. Explain that CSS can make Harry's web page look magical."
  },
  "published": true,
